  Extracted from the finished 171×24 wordmark grid rather than re-rastered, so
  its dot size and grid phase match static/assets/threesam-wordmark.svg exactly
  — the letter and the full mark are the same object at different crops.

  Sized in em off the parent's font-size: the viewBox's 24 rows are the whole
  word's ink height, which Michroma reports as 0.761em, and the negative bottom
  margin drops the box the 0.011em the word sits below the baseline so the glyph
  lands on the same baseline as the text letters beside it.

  Decorative here — BrandSignoff supplies the letter to the accessible name.
-->
